### Config — adjust if you changed ports
@keycloakUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiUrl = http://localhost:5080
@realm = multitenant-saas
@clientId = multitenant-saas-api

### 1. Get a token for Alice (tenant-admin @ Acme)
# @name aliceToken
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&username=alice&password=Passw0rd!

### 2. Get a token for Bob (tenant-member @ Acme)
# @name bobToken
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&username=bob&password=Passw0rd!

### 3. Get a token for Carol (tenant-admin @ Globex)
# @name carolToken
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&username=carol&password=Passw0rd!

### 4. Get a token for root (platform-admin, no tenant)
# @name rootToken
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&username=root&password=Passw0rd!

### 5. Who am I? (Alice) — should show Acme's tenant id + tenant-admin role
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 6. Alice creates a product in Acme
# @name createProduct
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Widget",
  "description": "A widget made by Acme",
  "price": 19.99,
  "stockQuantity": 100
}

### 7. Alice lists Acme's products — sees the widget
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 8. Carol (Globex) lists products — sees NOTHING (tenant isolation via global query filter)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{carolToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 9. Carol tries to fetch Acme's product by id directly — 404, not 403 (doesn't confirm it exists)
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{carolToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 10. Bob (tenant-member) tries to delete a product — 403, DELETE requires tenant-admin
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/api/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 11. root (platform-admin) lists all tenants — cross-tenant, requires platform-admin role
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{rootToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 12. Alice tries to list all tenants — 403, she's not a platform-admin
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken.response.body.access_token}}

### 13. root provisions a brand-new tenant
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{rootToken.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Initech",
  "slug": "initech"
}
